Sept 30, 2000

BOSS was modified to facilitate preparation of input structure files for
MCPRO. IF NEWZMAT = FULLM in the par file, the output plt.pdb file and
Z-matrix in the sum file will have the same unique PDB-input names for each
atom. The Z-matrix also has all AUTO entries expanded.

The script xSPM was also added to automate this. If you execute
xSPM inhibitor
a single-point force-field calculation will be performed on inhibitor.z
and the output plt.pdb and sum (Z-matrix) files will be prepared for MCPRO/pepz.

To do this, all atoms have three-character names. Previously, in the PDB file
atoms with 2-character atomic symbols like chlorine (Cl) had four-character names.
Some graphics programs (e.g. Midas) will process the 3-character symbols
correctly (Cl will be green), while others (e.g. RasMol) will not (Cl will
be grey like carbon). If you have BOSS write a .mol file, RasMol will display
it properly (xZmol inhbitor; rasmol -mdl inhibitor.mol).

